/* Pf013 - Entity-count amplification: tiny file, many GB resident
   Pattern A: many tiny entities each holding O(N) references; parser
              builds an O(N) instance pointer table AND an O(N^2) reverse-
              reference map. 50 MB of input -> 40+ GB resident.
   Pattern B (hub-style): millions of tiny entities all pointing at one
              HUB entity; contiguous-vector reverse-reference reallocation
              thrashes (A027, A040).
   Scaling-up: this stub illustrates the structure with ~20 points each
   referencing several neighbours, plus one HUB referenced by all. Scale
   to 5M points referencing 100 neighbours, or 10M tiny entities pointing
   at one hub, to trigger the reported 40 GB peak resident. */
